//# The protocols the checker holds an acquired resource to (spec §9
//# *Releasing resources*). A value of a `Release` type that a call returns
//# is the function's to give back: it defers a release of it, or
//# hands it on. A `Commit` type's release throws its work away, so a
//# function that defers that release commits on every path that returns
//# normally.

import {
    results.Result
    unit.Unit
}

/// A value that holds something outside the program, which a function that
/// acquires it gives back. The body of `release` names the type's usual
/// release, the call a `defer` after the acquisition makes:
///
/// ```nomi
/// impl Release for Writer {
///     fn release(w: Writer) {
///         Writer.discard(w)
///     }
/// }
/// ```
///
/// A value of the type that a call returns, directly or in a `Result` (an
/// acquisition: `fs.create`, `process.spawn`), is released in the function
/// that binds it: a `defer` of a call taking it, on the lines after the
/// binding, or it is returned or stored in a value that is.
pub interface Release {
    fn release(value: self) -> Unit
}

/// A `Release` type whose release discards the work done with the value,
/// and whose `commit` keeps it. The body of `commit` names the type's usual
/// commit:
///
/// ```nomi
/// impl Commit for Writer {
///     fn commit(w: Writer) -> Result<Unit, Error> {
///         Writer.close(w)
///     }
/// }
/// ```
///
/// A function that defers the discarding release of a Commit value calls the
/// commit on every path that returns normally: an `Ok` or `Some`, any other
/// value, or the end of a function that returns `Unit`.
pub interface Commit<E> {
    fn commit(value: self) -> Result<Unit, E>
}
